WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:02.830
- I was suffering from post
traumatic stress disorder,

00:00:02.830 --> 00:00:04.520
depression and grief.

00:00:04.520 --> 00:00:06.180
I was going downhill fast.

00:00:06.180 --> 00:00:09.390
- Ketamine's used as a
transformer of moods,

00:00:09.390 --> 00:00:11.180
only discovered in the late 90's.

00:00:11.180 --> 00:00:13.570
People were very incredulous,
it's an anesthetic,

00:00:13.570 --> 00:00:15.280
how could it have
anything to do with mood?

00:00:15.280 --> 00:00:17.130
- What is actually happening in the brain

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:18.400
when a person takes this drug?

00:00:18.400 --> 00:00:20.840
- I'm always a little
nervous before the injection

00:00:20.840 --> 00:00:23.400
'cause I know I have no
control over what my mind

00:00:23.400 --> 00:00:24.813
is going to think about.

00:00:34.540 --> 00:00:37.480
The trauma that I'm dealing
with, basically unthinkable

00:00:37.480 --> 00:00:40.623
but I've lost both of
my children to suicide.

00:00:40.840 --> 00:00:43.813
My youngest son, Dylan,
knew that his life mattered,

00:00:43.980 --> 00:00:46.210
that he mattered, that he had a voice

00:00:46.440 --> 00:00:48.963
and unfortunately, his impulsive nature,

00:00:49.270 --> 00:00:52.603
caused him to go in and shoot
himself and end his life.

00:00:53.259 --> 00:00:55.833
When I found him, I
screamed uncontrollably.

00:00:56.120 --> 00:00:58.033
What I saw, nobody should see.

00:00:59.730 --> 00:01:02.310
I ran out of the house
and then ran back in

00:01:02.610 --> 00:01:04.890
to make sure he wasn't still alive

00:01:04.890 --> 00:01:06.360
even though that's physically impossible

00:01:06.360 --> 00:01:08.053
based on what I looked at.

00:01:08.690 --> 00:01:10.120
I hired a grief counselor immediately,

00:01:10.120 --> 00:01:12.530
I hired the best post traumatic
stress disorder counselor

00:01:12.530 --> 00:01:15.030
I could find and I did
pull myself out of it,

00:01:15.030 --> 00:01:17.710
I did reengage and I had an older son

00:01:17.710 --> 00:01:20.800
who still lived with his
mum and I worried about him

00:01:20.800 --> 00:01:23.420
'cause he didn't go to
counseling and he held things in,

00:01:23.420 --> 00:01:25.770
he didn't share but he
kept saying he was fine.

00:01:26.720 --> 00:01:29.060
We were about to go to the
Edmonton Oilers playoff game

00:01:29.060 --> 00:01:31.290
with my dad and my sister
because I really believed

00:01:31.290 --> 00:01:33.430
in trying to united the
family, start having us

00:01:33.430 --> 00:01:36.433
live our lives again, that
was my obligation to others,

00:01:36.490 --> 00:01:39.023
friends and family and my son.

00:01:39.470 --> 00:01:42.103
My son was clearly
depressed but he denied it.

00:01:43.481 --> 00:01:45.480
And the day before he
was supposed to go back

00:01:45.480 --> 00:01:47.570
to see his mother, he
called me on a bike ride

00:01:47.570 --> 00:01:50.520
to tell me that he loved me
and I knew something was wrong.

00:01:52.520 --> 00:01:54.310
When he asked me how long I was gonna be,

00:01:54.310 --> 00:01:55.710
it reminded me of my other son

00:01:55.710 --> 00:01:57.483
when he asked me the same question.

00:02:00.220 --> 00:02:01.880
When I got home a year ago about today,

00:02:01.880 --> 00:02:04.413
I found my other son
dead of a gunshot wound.

00:02:06.881 --> 00:02:08.964
(crying)

00:02:13.200 --> 00:02:14.803
Needless to say, I fell apart.

00:02:16.090 --> 00:02:18.593
Brought in spiritual leaders,

00:02:18.970 --> 00:02:20.430
I brought in other counselors.

00:02:20.430 --> 00:02:23.430
Any ideas that people
had that could help me

00:02:24.210 --> 00:02:25.910
get a grip on my life 'cause

00:02:27.210 --> 00:02:28.730
for the first four months, I didn't care

00:02:28.730 --> 00:02:30.730
if I was alive, I didn't care if I died.

00:02:31.280 --> 00:02:33.380
I didn't think it mattered, I had no hope.

00:02:33.630 --> 00:02:34.923
I had no purpose.

00:02:35.250 --> 00:02:37.193
It was empty without my kids.

00:02:38.241 --> 00:02:40.824
(gentle music)

00:02:46.814 --> 00:02:48.800
I first went to some
grief recovery centers,

00:02:48.800 --> 00:02:50.680
I went to a brain scanning clinic.

00:02:50.680 --> 00:02:53.423
I signed up with an EMDR specialist.

00:02:53.550 --> 00:02:55.920
I was severely depressed
trying to get out of it

00:02:55.920 --> 00:02:57.830
and I wanted to try to make
some progress on my own

00:02:57.830 --> 00:02:59.580
before I came to do the ketamine

00:03:00.070 --> 00:03:01.600
and I wanted to get through Christmas.

00:03:01.600 --> 00:03:05.461
Having had lost one son
and knowing the worst date

00:03:05.461 --> 00:03:07.493
is Christmas, not the birthday,

00:03:07.530 --> 00:03:09.030
not the anniversary date of death,

00:03:09.030 --> 00:03:12.170
Christmas is the worst date
if you've lost a child.

00:03:12.170 --> 00:03:15.400
I knew I had that coming and
I didn't wanna be doing this

00:03:15.400 --> 00:03:17.450
or have just done it and
then get whacked again

00:03:17.450 --> 00:03:19.470
so I knew to get through Christmas.

00:03:19.470 --> 00:03:21.660
If I could get through
Christmas, early January,

00:03:21.660 --> 00:03:23.720
I'm flying back into
L.A., and I'm gonna come

00:03:23.720 --> 00:03:25.620
and spend two weeks and do this treatment.

00:03:25.620 --> 00:03:28.493
And I got through Christmas
and I made it here.

00:03:34.780 --> 00:03:38.210
- It's known as special
K, a psychedelic drug

00:03:38.210 --> 00:03:41.470
popular in dance clubs but
doctors say the same drug,

00:03:41.470 --> 00:03:45.510
ketamine, approved as animal
tranquilizer and anesthetic

00:03:45.600 --> 00:03:49.910
can also be a lifesaver when
used to treat severe depression

00:03:50.050 --> 00:03:51.730
when nothing else works.

00:03:51.730 --> 00:03:55.520
One small study found ketamine
decreased suicidal thoughts

00:03:55.520 --> 00:03:58.713
almost immediately in 50% of patients.

00:03:58.900 --> 00:04:01.443
Most anti-depressants take weeks.

00:04:01.660 --> 00:04:04.230
- Tom was pretty troubled
when he came to us.

00:04:04.230 --> 00:04:06.256
He was not dealing at all well.

00:04:06.256 --> 00:04:09.550
Tom really was blaming
himself a lot for that

00:04:09.710 --> 00:04:12.770
and was suffering a great
deal of guilt and remorse,

00:04:12.770 --> 00:04:15.620
pretty unsure about whether
he wanted to continue living.

00:04:15.780 --> 00:04:19.720
He had a very rough and
contentious first infusion.

00:04:19.720 --> 00:04:21.793
By the day after his second infusion,

00:04:22.310 --> 00:04:26.183
he was really just singing
the praises of the treatment.

00:04:26.250 --> 00:04:29.670
Ketamine was found to be a
profoundly effective anesthetic

00:04:29.670 --> 00:04:31.543
given as a lump or bolus.

00:04:31.630 --> 00:04:33.330
It was only when people began to give it

00:04:33.330 --> 00:04:36.800
in a very gradual way and
in sub-anesthetic doses

00:04:36.800 --> 00:04:39.270
that we realized what
an amazing mood elevator

00:04:39.270 --> 00:04:41.180
and reverser of suicidality it is.

00:04:41.180 --> 00:04:44.740
It starts a chain reaction,
it actually caused new growth

00:04:44.740 --> 00:04:47.830
in connections in the brain
and in receptor density

00:04:47.830 --> 00:04:49.073
among those connections.

00:04:49.250 --> 00:04:51.970
That patient, who has
an infusion, experiences

00:04:51.970 --> 00:04:55.190
a dissociative state, does
not have true hallucinations.

00:04:55.190 --> 00:04:57.150
He may see things that
aren't there but he knows

00:04:57.150 --> 00:04:58.313
that they're not there.

00:04:58.520 --> 00:05:02.190
Dissociation can be very
mild, like when you're waiting

00:05:02.190 --> 00:05:04.740
to pay at the grocery
store and you're thinking

00:05:04.740 --> 00:05:06.200
about what you're gonna do tonight,

00:05:06.200 --> 00:05:07.850
your mind and body are sort of separate.

00:05:07.850 --> 00:05:09.440
A lot of patients tell
us that they're able

00:05:09.440 --> 00:05:11.660
to do really important internal work

00:05:11.820 --> 00:05:13.230
while they're having an infusion.

00:05:13.230 --> 00:05:14.720
It can be really therapeutic for them

00:05:14.720 --> 00:05:18.080
to have a really objective
perspective on their life

00:05:18.090 --> 00:05:20.600
and this dissociation that
Dr. Mandel was talking about,

00:05:20.600 --> 00:05:22.610
of course, it's very
important, we're big advocates

00:05:22.610 --> 00:05:24.500
of talk therapy and for
them to work through

00:05:24.500 --> 00:05:26.100
some of these things with a professional.

00:05:26.100 --> 00:05:28.033
- It's a treatment, it's not a cure.

00:05:28.202 --> 00:05:30.420
It will not stand alone.

00:05:30.420 --> 00:05:32.400
- For me, I'm always a
little nervous before

00:05:32.400 --> 00:05:35.280
the injection 'cause I
know I have no control

00:05:35.280 --> 00:05:38.170
over what my mind is going to think about.

00:05:38.170 --> 00:05:40.660
It can go from very
pleasant to very scary.

00:05:40.660 --> 00:05:43.559
I know at the end, I'm
going to feel better.

00:05:43.559 --> 00:05:47.163
I'm gonna say it's an
out of body experience.

00:05:47.360 --> 00:05:49.990
I'm present watching myself but it's not

00:05:49.990 --> 00:05:52.130
in a dimension that I can explain.

00:05:52.130 --> 00:05:54.233
They actually let me know that I matter,

00:05:54.625 --> 00:05:56.500
that I am good enough.

00:05:56.500 --> 00:05:58.380
They gave me tools to discuss

00:05:58.380 --> 00:06:00.493
with my conventional psychologist.

00:06:01.740 --> 00:06:04.323
(gentle music)

00:06:18.220 --> 00:06:21.000
I had moments of emotional
pain from my loss

00:06:21.000 --> 00:06:24.083
that I understood why somebody
would wanna take their life.

00:06:24.270 --> 00:06:27.425
For whatever reason,
something changed in me

00:06:27.425 --> 00:06:30.270
that made me go from
I don't care if I live

00:06:30.270 --> 00:06:34.755
to I don't wanna die and now,
because of these treatments,

00:06:34.755 --> 00:06:39.470
I can now go and share my
story and let people know

00:06:39.470 --> 00:06:41.023
that life is worth living.

00:06:41.230 --> 00:06:43.400
That as bad as it gets,
as painful it gets,

00:06:43.400 --> 00:06:45.430
we do have a choice and we have freedom

00:06:45.430 --> 00:06:46.610
to make that choice.

00:06:46.610 --> 00:06:49.250
But I can go out and help
other people possibly

00:06:49.470 --> 00:06:51.750
and whether I'm successful
or not doesn't matter,

00:06:51.750 --> 00:06:53.480
I'm at least gonna try to do that.

00:06:53.480 --> 00:06:56.230
I'm gonna try to give back
what this clinic's given me.

00:06:56.670 --> 00:06:57.503
My life.

00:06:58.336 --> 00:07:00.919
(light music)

